Found 3 tool(s). Use DeferExecuteTool to invoke them.

## conversation_search
Search through past user conversations to find relevant context and information.
This tool can retrieve both Fact memories and Conversational memories.

### When to use this tool

Call this tool when historical user context could materially improve answer correctness, continuity, or personalization.
Do not call it when the answer is fully determined by current-turn input.

### How it works

The tool has ZERO access to the current conversation.
Your query MUST be self-contained: restate the current ask, specify what historical context is missing, and why it is needed.

### Examples of when to call this tool

- The user asks to continue prior work ("continue yesterday's task", "use previous decision", "same as last time").
- You need prior technical preferences (language/framework/testing style/deploy constraints) to give coding advice.
- You need prior work habits, recurring routines, or decision history for non-coding tasks (planning, writing, analysis, operations).
- The user references earlier constraints or commitments that affect current recommendations.

### How to write conversation_search queries

- Always write them as standalone messages -- the tool has no conversation view.
- Include current task context and target missing memory explicitly.
- If needed, mention both coding and general-work dimensions to broaden useful recall.

### Example queries

{"query": "User asks me to continue refactoring from last time. Find prior decisions about file boundaries, naming rules, and test strategy."}
{"query": "User asks for this week's work plan. Find past planning preferences, recurring priorities, and unfinished follow-ups from recent conversations."}
{"query": "I need the user's preferred response style and level of detail for technical vs non-technical tasks."}

Parameters:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "query"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "query": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A self-contained search query describing what historical context is needed. Must restate the current ask and specify what missing information to look for."
    },
    "start_date": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional start date for filtering conversations (ISO 8601 format, e.g. \"2026-03-01\"). Only conversations on or after this date will be searched."
    },
    "end_date": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional end date for filtering conversations (ISO 8601 format, e.g. \"2026-03-25\"). Only conversations on or before this date will be searched."
    },
    "limit": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Maximum number of results to return. Defaults to 5 if not provided."
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

## search_plugins
Read-only discovery for recommend-connectors and recommend-experts. Search available candidates that match the user's request — their pipeline, accounts, contracts, tickets, playbooks, or company data — when no existing tool covers it. Covers two categories via `type`: connector and expert. Returns real, currently valid candidates. Connector results include only Connectors not yet bound to the current account. A locally installed plugin does not mean this account has connected it. Bound Connectors are excluded even when disabled, disconnected, or awaiting reauthorization. Never installs, connects, or enables anything, and is the only source for candidates (do not use web search). When relevant candidates are returned, use a single suggest_plugin_install call to present up to three candidates in one card instead of listing them in text.

Parameters:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "type"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "connector",
        "expert"
      ],
      "description": "Candidate category to inspect: an external Connector, or an Expert (single expert or expert team)."
    },
    "userIntent": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The user's request in natural language. Pass it verbatim or lightly paraphrased — do not pre-tokenize it into keywords."
    },
    "keywords": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "description": "Optional keywords used to narrow candidates."
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

## suggest_plugin_install
Recommend Plugins to the user through an inline card in the message stream. The card can contain Connectors or Experts. Use this tool only after search_plugins has returned the candidates. IMPORTANT: this tool may be invoked at most once per response. Never emit two or more calls, including sequential or parallel calls; only one recommendation card can be pending in a session. To recommend multiple candidates, include 1–3 candidates of the same `type` in that call. The `type` must be connector or expert. Pass exact result `id` values in `pluginId1` and optional `pluginId2`/`pluginId3`; do not use arrays or an `item` wrapper. Example: `{ "type": "expert", "pluginId1": "ExpertA", "pluginId2": "ExpertB" }`.

Parameters:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "type",
    "pluginId1"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "connector",
        "expert"
      ],
      "description": "Card category. One call carries exactly one type and 1–3 candidates."
    },
    "contextLabel": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Short header tying the suggestion to what the user just asked about. 3–5 words, e.g. 'For your code repositories'."
    },
    "pluginId1": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "First exact `id` returned by this session's latest search_plugins call."
    },
    "pluginId2": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional second exact result `id`. Omit when recommending only one candidate."
    },
    "pluginId3": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional third exact result `id`. Omit when recommending fewer than three candidates."
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```
